{"audio":"voice-clean.mp3","hash":"c5db18b05ee73e72","durationSec":440.304,"text":"Payday hits. The rent's gone out. The bills are paid and there's some money left over. Maybe it's 200. Maybe it's a grand. Maybe you've built up 10 ,000 and Most people do one of two things with it. They leave it sitting in their current account and what do nothing or they wonder where it went. So in this video, I'm going to be showing you exactly what I would deal with 200 pounds a thousand pounds and 10 ,000 pounds in the right order. So your money actually starts working for you Before we get into the amounts you need to know the order because it doesn't matter how you much you've got if you put it into the wrong place. So step one clear expensive debt. If you've got a credit card and overdraft or a buy now pay later charging you about 20 % or more paying the office guaranteed return is a guaranteed return. No investment reliably beats that. Step two, start an emergency fund. Money and easy access savings account that you don't touch unless something goes wrong. And then step three, get your full employer pension match. If your work matches what you put in, that's free money. Don't leave it on the tape. And then step four, finish your emergency fund three to six months of essential living costs. Step five, invest for the long term ideally inside and nicer so you don't pay tax on the growth. Keep that lighter in your head because every amount we talk about today is just about how far up you can climb. Let's start with 200. And honestly, this is where most people are. So if this is you, you're in good company. If you've got expensive debt, put the lot towards it. Seriously, every pound you pay off is a pound that stops costing you about 20 % or more a year. If you're debt free, congratulations. Start with an emergency fund in an easy access account. So you can set up a standing order there every month after every day off the payday and move the money there before you can even spend it. That's the trick. Pay yourself first. And here's why 200 months, 200 pounds a month is about 2 ,400 a year. That alone could be a basic emergency fund for a lot of people. Once you've got a small buffer, even just a few hundred, you can start investing small. Most UK investing apps allow you to buy fractions of a fund. So you can start with as little as a few hundred pounds, you know, or 50 quid a month into a global index fund. And this is genuinely a good start. The point at this level is in demand. It's about building the habit. Now, let's say you've got a grand. First, same rule. If there's an expensive debt, that goes first. If not, a thousand pounds is a great milestone because it's enough to cover most small costs and most small emergencies. Car repair, broken phone. So my first move would be to make sure you've got at least a thousand pounds in your emergency fund. If you've already got that covered, here's where it gets interesting. If you're aged 18 to 39 and you're saving for your first home, then look into a lifetime ISO. You can put into up to four grand every year and the government adds about 25 % bonus. So put in a thousand pounds and you get a free 250 pounds on top of that. The catch, you can only use it for your first home as long as it costs 450 ,000 or less. Or once you hit 60. Take it out for anything else and you get a 25 % penalty, which actually leaves you a bit less than what you put in. So only use it if you're serious about buying a home. Not buying a home, then a Stocks and Shares ISO is going to be your best friend. Any growth and dividends inside of it are tax -free forever. Put your thousand into a low -cost global or S &P 500 index fund and leave it alone. And personally, this is what I'm doing, this is exactly what I'm doing on my Road to 100K Series. Emergency fund first, then index funds at its core. Okay, 10 ,000. If you've got this in your current account, I need you to hear this. It's losing value to inflation every single month. So let's put it to work. First, top up your emergency fund to three to six months of essential costs. If your essential costs are 1 ,500 a month, that's between 4 .5 and 9 ,000. Keep it somewhere easy to access that pays decent interest. Now, second, check your pension. Are you getting a full employer match? If not, increasing your contribution is often the best return available because you get a tax relief and your employer's money on top. Third, invest for the long term. A stock, essentially, as I saw, a low -cost index fund and time. Now, what you should not do with 10 grand. Put it all into one stock or into crypto because someone online said it's going to them in. Trust me, I learned the hard way. You don't want to do it. So that's the theory. Let me show you what I actually do because I don't want to just tell you what to do and start sharing you. Mine. Every payday, two things happen automatically before I can even think about spending it. A thousand pound goes straight into my savings. That's built me the emergency fund. And now it's going towards me buying my first home. And then 500 pounds goes straight into my S &P 500 index fund. I'm not timing the market. I'm not checking the news. It just goes straight in there every single month. And the key word there is that it's going to be just an automatic process. I set up a standing order for the day after payday. So the money goes straight in there before I even had the chance to talk myself out of it. That habit has done more for me for my finances than any other stock I've ever picked. Now, I know a thousand five hundred a month isn't completely realistic for everyone. That's completely fine. The amounts don't really matter as much as the system, whether it's 1500, 200 or 20. Care yourself first, automate it and let time do the work. And this is exactly what I'll be tracking every single month in my road to 100K series. So let's recap. Two hundred pounds, clear expensive debt, start your emergency fund and build the habit. A thousand pounds. Get to one grand, then a lifetime nicer if you're buying a home. If not, then your stocks and shares and then 10 ,000 complete your other emergency fund. Use your cash I saw allowance before April, grab your full pension match and invest the rest for the long term. Different amounts, same letter. You'll just climb me at all that different paces. So in the comments, I would like for you to tell me which one you are right now. Two hundred, a thousand or even 10 ,000. No judgment. Also, if you'd like to see how I'm doing all of this, I would love for you to check my road to 100K series.","words":[{"w":"Payday","s":1.49,"e":2.11},{"w":"hits.","s":2.11,"e":2.35},{"w":"The","s":2.67,"e":2.85},{"w":"rent's","s":2.85,"e":3.11},{"w":"gone","s":3.11,"e":3.23},{"w":"out.","s":3.23,"e":3.43},{"w":"The","s":3.81,"e":3.89},{"w":"bills","s":3.89,"e":4.07},{"w":"are","s":4.07,"e":4.21},{"w":"paid","s":4.21,"e":4.39},{"w":"and","s":4.39,"e":5.15},{"w":"there's","s":5.15,"e":5.35},{"w":"some","s":5.35,"e":5.45},{"w":"money","s":5.45,"e":5.61},{"w":"left","s":5.61,"e":5.77},{"w":"over.","s":5.77,"e":6.05},{"w":"Maybe","s":6.47,"e":6.71},{"w":"it's","s":6.71,"e":6.97},{"w":"200.","s":6.97,"e":7.15},{"w":"Maybe","s":7.65,"e":7.85},{"w":"it's","s":7.85,"e":8.07},{"w":"a","s":8.07,"e":8.13},{"w":"grand.","s":8.13,"e":8.27},{"w":"Maybe","s":8.73,"e":9.01},{"w":"you've","s":9.01,"e":9.25},{"w":"built","s":9.25,"e":9.41},{"w":"up","s":9.41,"e":9.51},{"w":"10","s":9.51,"e":9.69},{"w":",000","s":9.69,"e":9.99},{"w":"and","s":9.99,"e":10.69},{"w":"Most","s":10.69,"e":11.75},{"w":"people","s":11.75,"e":12.07},{"w":"do","s":12.07,"e":12.27},{"w":"one","s":12.27,"e":12.45},{"w":"of","s":12.45,"e":12.59},{"w":"two","s":12.59,"e":12.73},{"w":"things","s":12.73,"e":12.99},{"w":"with","s":12.99,"e":13.17},{"w":"it.","s":13.17,"e":13.31},{"w":"They","s":13.69,"e":13.87},{"w":"leave","s":13.87,"e":14.05},{"w":"it","s":14.05,"e":14.19},{"w":"sitting","s":14.19,"e"